From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:35:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] webconfig: publish mesh STA on connection change

The mesh-STA HAL connection indication updates OneWifi's authoritative VAP
cache, but the pending-response path encoded a generic `dml` document.  The
EasyMesh agent subscribes to the northbound WebConfig event and intentionally
dispatches only radio, fronthaul and mesh-STA documents; it logged the `dml`
document and ignored it.  A live backhaul reparent therefore changed the real
association while the agent and controller continued reporting the old BSSID.

Encode the mesh-STA subdocument for a mesh-STA connection-status response.
This publishes the BSSID that the HAL confirmed and lets the agent reconcile
its BSTA record and notify the controller without a process restart.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 source/core/wifi_ctrl_webconfig.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/core/wifi_ctrl_webconfig.c b/source/core/wifi_ctrl_webconfig.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/source/core/wifi_ctrl_webconfig.c
+++ b/source/core/wifi_ctrl_webconfig.c
@@ -553,7 +553,7 @@ int webconfig_state_machine(wifi_ctrl_t *ctrl)
             }
         break;
         case ctrl_webconfig_state_sta_conn_status_rsp_pending:
-            type = webconfig_subdoc_type_dml;
+            type = webconfig_subdoc_type_mesh_sta;
             webconfig_send_vap_subdoc_status(ctrl, type);
         break;
         case ctrl_webconfig_state_vap_mesh_sta_cfg_rsp_pending:
